  "result": "`drv.motion.stopping_distance` is written and the gate returned **OK** on its first run (1 of the 6-run budget). It ran 3 witnesses, and the concept reads one atom.\n\n- **Concept** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/stopping_distance.lean`): the value is the speed (`kin_speed(a)`) times `reaction_time`, plus the speed squared divided by `(2 · deceleration)`. The divisor uses only the deceleration parameter, never a measured value, as the language requires. `Units` has no constructor for a count, so the declared literal 2 is written `Units.ratio 2 1` with the `.count` tag. The contract fixes every term, so I declared no narrowings.\n- **Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/stopping_distance.lean`): the instance uses a 1 s reaction time and 5 m/s² deceleration, and expects the value between 0 m and 30 m. Each scene is one motor vehicle heading east:\n  - **holds:** at 10 m/s the value is 20 m, inside the bounds.\n  - **fails:** at 30 m/s the value is 120 m, above the 30 m limit.\n  - **blind:** the same scene as holds, with `kin.speed` left out of the manifest, gives unknown.\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory and records the gate run, the choices and why I finished.",
